{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/968711-help-me-list-things-a-student-or-faculty-member-might-have","id":968711,"title":"Help me list things a student or faculty member might have","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-13T13:39:25-07:00","id":968711,"title":"Help me list things a student or faculty member might have","content":"From what i'm told this game is going to take place at a University<br /> <br /> i'm suppose to pick between 6 and 8 items but would love to hear anything you can think of even if it well exceeds the expected number.<br /> \u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T13:47:27-07:00","id":968717,"title":"","content":"Smartphone, laptop, and a spare notebook are essential. You might also consider a good pair of sneakers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T14:12:15-07:00","id":968731,"title":"","content":"Backpack, notebooks, writing implements, smartphone, gun, laptop, assorted moneys.<br /> <br /> Depending on their focus they may have other things, art students may have a digital drawing tablet or art supplies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T14:20:58-07:00","id":968736,"title":"","content":"Laptop, subject notebooks and folders for each class, pens, pencils, highlighters, and post it flaggy things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T14:48:03-07:00","id":968752,"title":"","content":"Hip flask.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T14:52:56-07:00","id":968754,"title":"","content":"Slide calculator","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T15:25:31-07:00","id":968782,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all the suggestions, the GM won't tell us what kind of school it is or if it has a program for cooking, art, medicine, law, business, or music. So just general i guess. Any more suggestions would also be appreciated if you would like to share or continue to share ideas.<br /> <br /> Not sure if accessories count as more than 1 item so i put arrows next to some. Also the group voted to be assigned our characters randomly this time so i'm not sure if that's a factor.<br /> <br /> The list is subject to change, we aren't playing till this weekend but so far it contains:<br /> <br /> Wrist watch(waterproof, stop watch, alarm)<br /> Briefcase/Backpack<br /> Thermos<br /> Key Ring--&gt;Room Key--&gt;Car Key--&gt;Beeper(remote unlock, engine starter)<br /> Laptop--&gt;Charger<br /> Smart Phone--&gt;Charger<br /> Digital drawing tablet--&gt;Charger<br /> Wallet--&gt;Credit cards--&gt;Library card--&gt;License--&gt;Student/Work I.D.<br /> <br /> <br /> i thought about listing a map of the campus but wasn't sure if that'd be considered cheating","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12063,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","user":"Seta143","date":". 09-15-2016, 01:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T17:47:58-07:00","id":968863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seta143</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/968711-help-me-list-things-a-student-or-faculty-member-might-have?p=968782#post968782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for all the suggestions, the GM won't tell us what kind of school it is or if it has a program for cooking, art, medicine, law, business, or music. So just general i guess. Any more suggestions would also be appreciated if you would like to share or continue to share ideas.<br /> <br /> Not sure if accessories count as more than 1 item so i put arrows next to some. Also the group voted to be assigned our characters randomly this time so i'm not sure if that's a factor.<br /> <br /> The list is subject to change, we aren't playing till this weekend but so far it contains:<br /> <br /> Wrist watch(waterproof)<br /> Briefcase/Backpack<br /> Thermos<br /> Car keys--&gt;Beeper<br /> Laptop--&gt;Charger<br /> Cell phone--&gt;Charger<br /> Digital drawing tablet--&gt;Charger<br /> Wallet--&gt;Credit cards--&gt;Library card--&gt;License<br /> <br /> <br /> i thought about listing a map of the campus but wasn't sure if that'd be considered cheating</div> </div> </div> </div>In my experience, that's unnecessary after the first week of classes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T18:50:46-07:00","id":968910,"title":"","content":"Don't forget coffee, instant macaroni, and desperation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T21:58:29-07:00","id":969014,"title":"","content":"A map may be unnecessary after the first week but on that first day, when you show up at class ten minutes before it starts only to find a paper taped to the door announcing that your freshman level class has been moved to the Chemistry building, a building that says Widsoe Hall on the outside, not Chemistry building, you really wish you had a map. Especially if that class is at seven thirty in the morning and there isn't much of anyone around to ask directions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T14:57:46-07:00","id":969477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/968711-help-me-list-things-a-student-or-faculty-member-might-have?p=969014#post969014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A map may be unnecessary after the first week but on that first day, when you show up at class ten minutes before it starts only to find a paper taped to the door announcing that your freshman level class has been moved to the Chemistry building, a building that says Widsoe Hall on the outside, not Chemistry building, you really wish you had a map. Especially if that class is at seven thirty in the morning and there isn't much of anyone around to ask directions.</div> </div> </div> </div> But then you might miss out on the joys of getting lost, that in itself could make for a great adventure<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T16:11:27-07:00","id":969510,"title":"","content":"In addition to things mentioned, a fancy overpriced graphing calculator... and enough heavy overpriced textbooks to make a good improvised weapon. There may be other specific things depending on the characters major.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T16:15:10-07:00","id":969512,"title":"","content":"If the character is female, mace, maxi pads (good bandages), a mirror, makeup kit, barrets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":4046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","user":"xenoterracide","date":". 09-14-2016, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T16:28:02-07:00","id":969517,"title":"","content":"In wallet don't forget a student Id, just in case campus security asks, and I don't think having a wrinkled up map in the bottom of your backpack is cheating","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T21:00:14-07:00","id":969641,"title":"","content":"Not everything they have will directly relate to school. Their lives and interests, even dorm living freshmen, extend beyond the campus.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T22:34:10-07:00","id":969671,"title":"","content":"The other factor to consider is i might not end up being a student since we are picking our characters out of a hat. Which could result in teacher, janitor, or other faculty member.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12063,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","user":"Seta143","date":". 09-15-2016, 01:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T23:18:50-07:00","id":969691,"title":"","content":"If you get the janitor then you will have the keys to the kingdom (or at least to every door in one building).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T08:50:26-07:00","id":969947,"title":"","content":"i'll probably be happy as long as i don't get stuck with campus security guy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T17:39:17-07:00","id":970338,"title":"","content":"That would depend on wither or not the uniform came with a red shirt. Otherwise you might be the only one in the game who is both openly armed and carrying master keys for much of the campus, certainly the more public buildings.<br /> \u200bYou would also have the advantage that only those with authority would question your presence or all but the most extreme actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T17:52:36-07:00","id":970350,"title":"","content":"Teacher will have similar items to a student, but they will also have keys to places like the staff lounge, and it depend on a teacher of what. If you can choose I'd go with chemistry (you may not be carrying dangerous chemicals but you know about them) or perhaps a class that excuses you to invest in occult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T19:32:05-07:00","id":970412,"title":"","content":"Members of the faculty usually have their own private libraries (my supervisor has a few hundred books in his office alone on his area of research) and definitely their favourite vice (usually coffee, wine or beer). Having access to &quot;secure&quot; offices of their own usually helps too. Faculty members usually have access to staff time in some capacity and their students would count for that too! They have computers, the ability to avoid or join meetings at a whim. Depending on the University, they'd have access to resources due to status too. Faculty members usually have priority access to equipment directly related to their research (my supervisor for instance had priority access to the NMR spectrometer when he was actively running structural research). Staff members in general usually have 24 hour access to the campus buildings that they belong to, too - be it building keys or NFC keycards coded to let them in. Most of the faculty avoid carrying around much stuff because they've got storage space, they're likely to just have the basics when they're out and about like a phone and a small bag with an organiser, diary, access cards, car keys, etc.<br /> <br /> PhD students have similar access to faculty, but far less &quot;pull&quot; - they're usually in a shared office (the entire research group under one supervisor is usually in one room), they quite often get all-hours access, they sometimes get junior honours/masters students that they have to mentor (but in exchange can act as staff for them too). They'll have less resources by far (most of it is by grace of the institution and their supervisors), but otherwise they still have significant access. PhDs/Masters students tend to get access to speciality equipment by their research and tend to carry around stuff they don't want left unsupervised in their common offices (have known more than a few of my PhD friends who don't leave their laptops in their shared office for exactly that reason).<br /> <br /> Undergraduates are likely to be the people who carry tonnes of crap around - most don't get storage areas (or they're really temporary) so you'll find them with folders, notes, books, laptops, etc. as normal course of their day. They're also likely to carry around any hobby stuff they're doing, most likely to have snacks on them as individuals. They'll often have spare clothes (e.g. they're science students and have lab coats/glasses or they've got part-time jobs and need a chance of clothes for work). Things like printed bus/train schedules are pretty common, as are maps early in the semester.<br /> <br /> Basically, treat anyone that's of faculty or PhD/Masters as someone who lives at the University - they've got office space and can and will store things there rather than carry them on their person. Comparatively, undergrads are basically permanent visitors - they'll always be lugging lots of stuff around and have everything they need for their uni day on them.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> On the subject of available staff, I'll list what I had access to as a PhD student and could request tasks/resources from - it's actually quite a bit! I'd also provide a guess of what skill they'd be appropriate for.<br /> <br /> Junior Students (Science)<br /> Research Librarian (Academics)<br /> School Administration (Politics)<br /> Laboratory Managers and Technical Staff (Craft)<br /> Research Association (Socialise)<br /> Campus Security (Investigation)<br /> Counselling Service (Empathy?)<br /> Medical Practice (Medicine)<br /> <br /> A lot of these I didn't have access to as an undergraduate, so they're definitely something that you could make use of with higher status at a University, or by having explicit staff from the Merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1462,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","user":"Xenesis","date":". 09-15-2016, 10:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T21:23:44-07:00","id":970475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/968711-help-me-list-things-a-student-or-faculty-member-might-have?p=970338#post970338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would depend on wither or not the uniform came with a red shirt. Otherwise you might be the only one in the game who is both openly armed and carrying master keys for much of the campus, certainly the more public buildings.<br /> \u200bYou would also have the advantage that only those with authority would question your presence or all but the most extreme actions.</div> </div> </div> </div> i don't like the idea of having that much of an advantage over the rest of the group, from my perspective doing more with less usually results in more fun and commands more respect.<br /> <br /> That and combat type characters excepts for ones like Joxer from Xena are usually less appealing to me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T23:56:36-07:00","id":970539,"title":"","content":"If you don't mind looking at it like a player with meta knowledge, while still staying within the bounds of the reasonable, I would recommend three things no matter what role you draw.<br /> \u200b1-A pocket knife, I'm talking a less than two inch long blade utility knife.<br /> 2-A multi-tool, yea they're crap compared to a dedicated tool but it would allow you to at least attempt tasks that require a tool.<br /> 3-A mini mag light of some sort. Never underestimate the usefulness, even in normal light, of having a small light source handy. After 40 you often need one just to see into shadows.<br /> All of these are things 'real' people carry on a regular basis and while they might be hard to fit into the pockets of your blue jeans they will easily fit in jacket pockets or the standard backpack. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T10:49:55-07:00","id":971401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seta143</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/968711-help-me-list-things-a-student-or-faculty-member-might-have?p=970475#post970475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i don't like the idea of having that much of an advantage over the rest of the group, from my perspective doing more with less usually results in more fun and commands more respect.<br /> <br /> That and combat type characters excepts for ones like Joxer from Xena are usually less appealing to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>afaik campus security isn't likely to carry a gun, but they might carry a bigger mace, or maybe a taser (even then I'm dubious). Keep in mind they're basically mall cops, their to take incident reports really, maybe break up fights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T21:15:28-07:00","id":971741,"title":"","content":"There are actually two levels of security, at least on campuses in my state, there are the guys in shirts that say 'SECURITY' that stand at doors and in halls during events to make sure you bought a ticket, and there are Campus Police, real police who went through the Academy, carry a real badge, have the authority to make arrests sending you through the city/state court system, and also investigate rapes and violent assaults.<br /> \u200bIf I were the ST I would only allow players to have this role if I knew my story was one that couldn't quickly be solved by someone with a badge and gun. Classic Horror is filled with scenarios were the monster won't fall to simple bullets, the protagonists don't have the option of calling for support and the monster in question doesn't care about no stinking badges.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T21:21:33-07:00","id":971745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/968711-help-me-list-things-a-student-or-faculty-member-might-have?p=971741#post971741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are actually two levels of security, at least on campuses in my state, there are the guys in shirts that say 'SECURITY' that stand at doors and in halls during events to make sure you bought a ticket, and there are Campus Police, real police who went through the Academy, carry a real badge, have the authority to make arrests sending you through the city/state court system, and also investigate rapes and violent assaults.<br /> \u200bIf I were the ST I would only allow players to have this role if I knew my story was one that couldn't quickly be solved by someone with a badge and gun. Classic Horror is filled with scenarios were the monster won't fall to simple bullets, the protagonists don't have the option of calling for support and the monster in question doesn't care about no stinking badges.</div> </div> </div> </div>probably depends on the campus, are we talking university? community college? trade school? etc. I've not encountered these types of police at my school, but I didn't go to a university.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T21:52:41-07:00","id":971759,"title":"","content":"University, though admittedly it wasn't always like that. Back in the early 90's issues involving jurisdiction, involving campus and not, led to the state adopting a system were even a small town cop had jurisdiction in a city on the far side of the state and campus police departments were created to ease the problem of enforcing the law on people even after they leave campus. It even crosses bordering state lines, an officer making an arrest outside his nominal area still surrenders the case and offender to the locals but gone are arguments of wither he had the right to make the arrest in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T22:13:27-07:00","id":971770,"title":"","content":"I would also try to keep from kneecapping yourself too much the GM has probably created these different role's to ensure that you've got someone equipped to handle X. Having a weapon as security might make you the only armed person, and the GM might be relying on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T12:57:42-07:00","id":972083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seta143</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/968711-help-me-list-things-a-student-or-faculty-member-might-have?p=970475#post970475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i don't like the idea of having that much of an advantage over the rest of the group, from my perspective doing more with less usually results in more fun and commands more respect.<br /> <br /> That and combat type characters excepts for ones like Joxer from Xena are usually less appealing to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not necessarily a net advantage, at least when you look at the other characters' abilities and resources. A campus cop may have a gun and access to campus buildings, but he's going to be lacking in academic resources. Even if they're actual police (which the ones on my smallish state university are), their authority is limited to law enforcement. They don't have much political pull with the administration or faculty beyond that scope, and they don't have access to the resources that faculty would in terms of equipment, a library, student assistance, etc. And even a student might have advantages in certain situations. Students are more likely to be more open when talking to other students than with faculty or police, and there may be parts of the campus that are known to students that the faculty and staff aren't aware of, or at least places they wouldn't think of going, such as <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roof_and_tunnel_hacking\" target=\"_blank\">rooftops and steam tunnels</a>. There are also a lot of social situations in which a student would fit in better than faculty or staff. (Unless you're that rare &quot;cool&quot; professor, showing up at the homecoming bonfire would get you a lot of awkward looks as faculty, and you'd definitely be looking in from the outside as a campus cop.)<br /> <br /> So being the only member of the group with a weapon is definitely an advantage, there are definitely plenty of areas where you'd be at a disadvantage, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12354,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12354-who-is-matt","user":"who.is.matt","date":". 09-18-2016, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12354-who-is-matt","name":"who.is.matt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T13:07:13-07:00","id":973331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/968711-help-me-list-things-a-student-or-faculty-member-might-have?p=971741#post971741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are actually two levels of security, at least on campuses in my state, there are the guys in shirts that say 'SECURITY' that stand at doors and in halls during events to make sure you bought a ticket, and there are Campus Police, real police who went through the Academy, carry a real badge, have the authority to make arrests sending you through the city/state court system, and also investigate rapes and violent assaults.</div> </div> </div> </div>At every school I've ever attended or worked at (and I've only been at traditional colleges and universities, never a trade school or similar, so I can't speak for those), Campus Police filled both of those roles, and they were actual police officers, and they carried (and carry) guns on campus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T14:31:17-07:00","id":973391,"title":"","content":"Ramen packets.<br /> Dirty unwashed dishes.<br /> Hamper full of dirty clothes.<br /> Ah this list reminds me of my college days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T14:37:50-07:00","id":973395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/968711-help-me-list-things-a-student-or-faculty-member-might-have?p=970412#post970412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Members of the faculty usually have their own private libraries (my supervisor has a few hundred books in his office alone on his area of research) and definitely their favourite vice (usually coffee, wine or beer). Having access to &quot;secure&quot; offices of their own usually helps too. Faculty members usually have access to staff time in some capacity and their students would count for that too! They have computers, the ability to avoid or join meetings at a whim. Depending on the University, they'd have access to resources due to status too. Faculty members usually have priority access to equipment directly related to their research (my supervisor for instance had priority access to the NMR spectrometer when he was actively running structural research). Staff members in general usually have 24 hour access to the campus buildings that they belong to, too - be it building keys or NFC keycards coded to let them in. Most of the faculty avoid carrying around much stuff because they've got storage space, they're likely to just have the basics when they're out and about like a phone and a small bag with an organiser, diary, access cards, car keys, etc.<br /> <br /> PhD students have similar access to faculty, but far less &quot;pull&quot; - they're usually in a shared office (the entire research group under one supervisor is usually in one room), they quite often get all-hours access, they sometimes get junior honours/masters students that they have to mentor (but in exchange can act as staff for them too). They'll have less resources by far (most of it is by grace of the institution and their supervisors), but otherwise they still have significant access. PhDs/Masters students tend to get access to speciality equipment by their research and tend to carry around stuff they don't want left unsupervised in their common offices (have known more than a few of my PhD friends who don't leave their laptops in their shared office for exactly that reason).<br /> <br /> Undergraduates are likely to be the people who carry tonnes of crap around - most don't get storage areas (or they're really temporary) so you'll find them with folders, notes, books, laptops, etc. as normal course of their day. They're also likely to carry around any hobby stuff they're doing, most likely to have snacks on them as individuals. They'll often have spare clothes (e.g. they're science students and have lab coats/glasses or they've got part-time jobs and need a chance of clothes for work). Things like printed bus/train schedules are pretty common, as are maps early in the semester.<br /> <br /> Basically, treat anyone that's of faculty or PhD/Masters as someone who lives at the University - they've got office space and can and will store things there rather than carry them on their person. Comparatively, undergrads are basically permanent visitors - they'll always be lugging lots of stuff around and have everything they need for their uni day on them.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> On the subject of available staff, I'll list what I had access to as a PhD student and could request tasks/resources from - it's actually quite a bit! I'd also provide a guess of what skill they'd be appropriate for.<br /> <br /> Junior Students (Science)<br /> Research Librarian (Academics)<br /> School Administration (Politics)<br /> Laboratory Managers and Technical Staff (Craft)<br /> Research Association (Socialise)<br /> Campus Security (Investigation)<br /> Counselling Service (Empathy?)<br /> Medical Practice (Medicine)<br /> <br /> A lot of these I didn't have access to as an undergraduate, so they're definitely something that you could make use of with higher status at a University, or by having explicit staff from the Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good list. Just to add, adjuncts sometimes also have to share offices. And if you're someone with grading responsibilities (a professor or a PhD student, and sometimes MA students), remember that it's a FERPA violation to leave graded papers in unlocked containers, or on your desk for students to pick up unless they're sealed in envelopes with the student's name. I say this because it means that just about every university (every one where I've seen offices) provides locked containers to faculty, including individual locked containers when offices are shared by graduate students.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T15:01:13-07:00","id":973414,"title":"","content":"Just look at what you have in your pockets and car right now, odds are most of it is the same for a University student. If you are carrying it then odds are real life taught you it was useful to have on short notice, if it's in your car than its probably something you have found useful to have even away from home. Beyond that about all a student (or faculty) have that you don't is a backpack and text books. Odds are you even own a pencil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T19:43:02-07:00","id":973598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/968711-help-me-list-things-a-student-or-faculty-member-might-have?p=973395#post973395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if you're someone with grading responsibilities (a professor or a PhD student, and sometimes MA students), remember that it's a FERPA violation to leave graded papers in unlocked containers, or on your desk for students to pick up unless they're sealed in envelopes with the student's name. I say this because it means that just about every university (every one where I've seen offices) provides locked containers to faculty, including individual locked containers when offices are shared by graduate students.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually had no idea that this was a thing, because there isn't something that exists similarly in Australia. I've marked reports and papers for years and never had to deal with any explicit locked storage for confidentiality reasons. I was even generally permitted to return marked work from a pile that can simply be collected by the individual students. I mean, I had a lockable drawer, but that's not exactly hard to get into. And uncollected reports are generally just kept with the student laboratory manager to be picked up (or ignored) as desired on a shelf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1462,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","user":"Xenesis","date":". 09-20-2016, 10:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T20:34:46-07:00","id":973614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/968711-help-me-list-things-a-student-or-faculty-member-might-have?p=973598#post973598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually had no idea that this was a thing, because there isn't something that exists similarly in Australia. I've marked reports and papers for years and never had to deal with any explicit locked storage for confidentiality reasons. I was even generally permitted to return marked work from a pile that can simply be collected by the individual students. I mean, I had a lockable drawer, but that's not exactly hard to get into. And uncollected reports are generally just kept with the student laboratory manager to be picked up (or ignored) as desired on a shelf.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the US, it's sometimes done this way, but it's considered a FERPA violation (or a privacy violation, if you're unfamiliar with FERPA) and the school can be sued. The idea is that once a paper is graded, it's no longer a student assignment, it is now a student record.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T20:41:08-07:00","id":973617,"title":"","content":"As another Australian, that seems really strange to me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The majority of my reports and assignments were normally given to a student down near the front and then handed back with the student walking about the room. Most folks made fun of one another for our marks. Privacy never really entered our minds <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T12:18:57-07:00","id":973966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gullinbursti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/968711-help-me-list-things-a-student-or-faculty-member-might-have?p=973617#post973617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As another Australian, that seems really strange to me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The majority of my reports and assignments were normally given to a student down near the front and then handed back with the student walking about the room. Most folks made fun of one another for our marks. Privacy never really entered our minds <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>FERPA is the privacy law that deals with education. HIPAA, which deals with the privacy of medical records, is very similar. They both require that &quot;reasonable methods&quot; be used to protect the individual's privacy. The locked container issue mostly comes up when you have graduate assistants who don't have actual offices but are tasked with grading assignments. As a college instructor, I'm fine leaving papers on my desk in my office while I'm in class, assuming I lock my office door while I'm out, since that's a &quot;reasonable&quot; measure to prevent unauthorized people from getting hold of those papers. <br /> <br /> If you really want to know more, check out <a href=\"http://www.ucop.edu/general-counsel/_files/ed-affairs/ferpa101.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">this summary</a>.<br /> <br /> And that's only really when you're dealing with physical records. With digital records, it's mostly about encryption. Since I use my laptop for work, I have to make sure my hard drive is encrypted so that if someone steals my laptop they can't access the students' records. So that's something else that might be important: if the chronicle is set in the US and a character is a faculty member, someone shouldn't be able to just pick up and use their laptop or phone (assuming the character cares about keeping his job). Any device he uses for work purposes would be fully encrypted, requiring a password or PIN to access.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12354-who-is-matt","name":"who.is.matt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}